            <ArticleTitle>Palliative treatment of Erdheim-Chester disease with radiotherapy: a Rare Cancer Network study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>323-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A retrospective study of the use of palliative external beam radiotherapy (EBRT) in nine patients with Erdheim-Chester disease was conducted through the Rare Cancer Network. Patients received EBRT for bone pain, brain infiltration, or retro-orbital involvement. EBRT typically provided short-term palliation, with later recurrence of symptoms in most cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
